\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Configuration Clifford algebras}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{Quadratic energy assigns a number to each field. Can this form
also be encoded by products of field generators? The
[configuration quadratic form](fdip-000O) determines a
[Clifford algebra](fdip-000P) through its square relation.
Keeping the polar normalization explicit lets
[form-preserving maps](fdip-000Q) act functorially, without identifying
a quadratic map with a chosen coordinate array. This algebra encodes
the supplied configuration form; it does not choose the spatial
Clifford module used for [Dirac operators](fdip-001C).}

\transclude{fdip-000O}
\transclude{fdip-000P}
\transclude{fdip-000Q}
